	(text "6-PLANT WATERING SYSTEM - YD-ESP32-23 (ESP32-S3)\nSENSORS (ADC1, direct): S1=IO1 S2=IO2 S3=IO7 S4=IO8 S5=IO9 S6=IO10 | SENSOR DIS (shared): IO11\nPUMPS: PUMP1=IO15 PUMP2=IO17 PUMP3=IO39 PUMP4=IO12 PUMP5=IO16 PUMP6=IO18 (named after the channel each pin drives)\nUI MODULE (same pins as breathing-light firmware): SDA=IO14 SCL=IO13 CON=IO21 PSH=IO6 TRA=IO5 TRB=IO4 BAK=IO38; VCC=3V3 (not 5V)\nAvoid IO0 IO3 IO45 IO46 (strapping), IO19/20 (USB), IO35-37 (octal PSRAM on N16R8), IO43/44 (UART)\nGate network: 220R series + 10k pull-down. Flyback diode across each pump.\nPOWER: USB-C 5V/2A charger -> +5V rail -> (ESP 5V pin) and (MT3608 boost -> +12V for pumps). ESP 3V3 pin feeds sensors + UI module.\nRun ONE pump at a time (firmware). Pump ~0.17A @12V = ~0.5A from 5V. Set MT3608 trim to 12V BEFORE connecting anything.\nC5 470uF on 5V absorbs pump start-up current; soft-start pump with PWM if the ESP resets.\nFLOAT SWITCH (optional, reservoir low-water lockout): J15 pin1 -> IO47 (use INPUT_PULLUP in firmware), pin2 -> GND. Leave unpopulated if unused.\nPS1 footprint = MT3608 module HW-183B (30x17mm, USB-C input), 4 corner holes, spacing 23.4 x 12.7 mm ESTIMATED from photo: measure your module and fix the footprint before ordering. VIN+ top-left, VIN- bottom-left, OUT+ top-right, OUT- bottom-right.\nESP 5V pin: vendor schematic has a Schottky from pin 21 to the on-board LDO (keep IN-OUT jumper open). Some YD units wire pin 21 as 3V3 - measure before connecting +5V!"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 265 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "02ea0457-e3c4-4ed4-a33d-01953193396a")
	)
